{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba test/yin/vm/linker_test.cljc | sed -n '140,166p;1060,1132p'\nnl -ba docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md | sed -n '280,315p;408,450p;1348,1378p'\nnl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc | sed -n '54,73p'\ngit status --short\ngit diff HEAD --check\nawk 'length(\"'$0)>80 {print FNR \":\" length($0)}'\"' src/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc test/yin/vm/linker_test.cljc | head -20\nLC_ALL=C rg -n '[\"'^'\"\\\\x00-\\\\x7F]' src/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc test/yin/vm/linker_test.cljc | head -20\"","aggregated_output":"   140\t\n   141\t\n   142\t(def ^:private yin-def-reads-its-own-name\n   143\t  \"`((fn [_ _] 0) (yin/def x x))`: the value operand reads `x`, and the\n   144\t   walker evaluates the operands before it calls `yin/def` -- the read\n   145\t   precedes the definition recorded at the invocation position.\"\n   146\t  (app (lam '[a b] (lit 0))\n   147\t       (app (v 'yin/def) (lit 'x) (v 'x))))\n   148\t\n   149\t\n   150\t(def ^:private yin-def-rebound-then-apparent-def\n   151\t  \"`((fn [_ _ _ _] 0) (vm/store-put k 1) (yin/def yin/def 0)\n   152\t     (yin/def x 1) x)`: the module rebinds `yin/def`, and runtime\n   153\t   resolution checks the active store before the primitives -- so the\n   154\t   later apparent definition of `x` calls the store's binding, not the\n   155\t   `yin/def` primitive, and is not provably a store.\"\n   156\t  (app (lam '[a b c d] (lit 0))\n   157\t       (store-put 'k 1)\n   158\t       (app (v 'yin/def) (lit 'yin/def) (lit 0))\n   159\t       (app (v 'yin/def) (lit 'x) (lit 1))\n   160\t       (v 'x)))\n   161\t\n   162\t\n   163\t(def ^:private scan-vector\n   164\t  \"A hand-built canonical vector: an unconditional binding, one inside a\n   165\t   jump's target range, a call site, and a closure body reading `w`.\"\n   166\t  [[:store-put 'y 1]     ; 0 unconditional\n  1060\t                                              (mint def-then-use))\n  1061\t            res (linker/fetch store index format identity)]\n  1062\t        (is (linker/ok? res))\n  1063\t        (is (= [] (:obligations res))\n  1064\t            \"the unconditional definition dominating the read discharges\n  1065\t             it: the image is closed\")\n  1066\t        (jing/close! store)))))\n  1067\t\n  1068\t\n  1069\t(deftest a-constant-key-yin-def-application-is-a-definition\n  1070\t  (let [store (mem/create-content-mem)\n  1071\t        tree (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode yin-def-then-read)\n  1072\t        root (:root tree)\n  1073\t        {:keys [identity index]} (publish store linker/ast-format tree)]\n  1074\t    (is (= [{:name 'x, :at [root [[3 0] [3 2]]], :conditional? false}]\n  1075\t           ((:definitions-fn linker/ast-format) tree))\n  1076\t        \"the constant-key yin/def application is a definition at its\n  1077\t         invocation position -- the application row's path extended one\n  1078\t         step past its operands, where the walker applies the operator\")\n  1079\t    (let [res (linker/fetch store index linker/ast-format identity\n  1080\t                            receiver)]\n  1081\t      (is (linker/ok? res))\n  1082\t      (is (= '[yin/def] (mapv :name (:obligations res)))\n  1083\t          \"the read after the binding is discharged, not a false free\n  1084\t           obligation; the yin/def operator stays an obligation the\n  1085\t           receiver resolves through its primitives\"))\n  1086\t    (jing/close! store)))\n  1087\t\n  1088\t\n  1089\t(deftest a-yin-def-value-operand-read-precedes-the-definition\n  1090\t  (let [store (mem/create-content-mem)\n  1091\t        tree (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode yin-def-reads-its-own-name)\n  1092\t        root (:root tree)\n  1093\t        {:keys [identity index]} (publish store linker/ast-format tree)]\n  1094\t    (is (= [{:name 'x, :at [root [[3 0] [3 2]]], :conditional? false}]\n  1095\t           ((:definitions-fn linker/ast-format) tree))\n  1096\t        \"the binding is recorded at the invocation position, one step\n  1097\t         past the two operands\")\n  1098\t    (is (= {:status :refused, :reason :use-before-definition, :name 'x}\n  1099\t           (select-keys (linker/fetch store index linker/ast-format\n  1100\t                                      identity receiver)\n  1101\t                        [:status :reason :name]))\n  1102\t        \"the walker evaluates the value operand before it calls\n  1103\t         yin/def, so the read of x inside it precedes the definition\n  1104\t         and is not discharged: :use-before-definition\")\n  1105\t    (jing/close! store)))\n  1106\t\n  1107\t\n  1108\t(deftest a-module-that-rebinds-yin-def-discharges-nothing-from-it\n  1109\t  (let [store (mem/create-content-mem)\n  1110\t        tree (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode yin-def-rebound-then-apparent-def)\n  1111\t        root (:root tree)\n  1112\t        {:keys [identity index]} (publish store linker/ast-format tree)]\n  1113\t    (is (= [{:name 'k, :at [root [[3 0]]], :conditional? false}]\n  1114\t           ((:definitions-fn linker/ast-format) tree))\n  1115\t        \"with yin/def in the module's own footprint no apparent\n  1116\t         definition is provably the primitive: every yin/def-derived\n  1117\t         binding is dropped, fail-closed, and only the store-put\n  1118\t         binding survives\")\n  1119\t    (is (= {:status :refused, :reason :unresolved-free, :name 'x}\n  1120\t           (select-keys (linker/fetch store index linker/ast-format\n  1121\t                                      identity receiver)\n  1122\t                        [:status :reason :name]))\n  1123\t        \"the apparent definition discharges nothing, so the read of x\n  1124\t         keeps its obligation, and the receiver -- which resolves the\n  1125\t         yin/def operators through its primitives -- cannot resolve x\")\n  1126\t    (jing/close! store)))\n  1127\t\n  1128\t\n  1129\t(deftest a-use-before-every-definition-is-use-before-definition\n  1130\t  (doseq [[label format mint] formats]\n  1131\t    (testing label\n  1132\t      (let [store (mem/create-content-mem)\n   280\t  row ids of a row body.\n   281\t- `:obligations-fn`, `:definitions-fn`, and `:applications-fn` are\n   282\t  **position-bearing scanners** with one shared result shape:\n   283\t\n   284\t  ```clojure\n   285\t  ;; :obligations-fn  value -> [{:name sym :at position :in-body? b}]\n   286\t  ;; :definitions-fn  value -> [{:name sym :at position\n   287\t  ;;                             :conditional? b}]\n   288\t  ;; :applications-fn value -> [{:at position}]\n   289\t  ;; position: a tree occurrence path [root-address path] for\n   290\t  ;;           :yin.ast/code; a pc for the vector formats\n   291\t  ```\n   292\t\n   293\t  `:conditional?` is true when any `:if` branch, jump target range, or\n   294\t  lambda body encloses the definition; `:in-body?` is true when a\n   295\t  lambda body encloses the occurrence; an `:applications-fn` record is\n   296\t  one **application site**: a position at which this image may apply a\n   297\t  closure it creates -- a direct call site, a call of an imported\n   298\t  name, or a call of a primitive that receives a function argument,\n   299\t  because the callee may apply what it is handed. Dominance between\n   300\t  two positions is decided by the linker from these fields and the\n   301\t  format's order (step 5a). For the AST record all three scanners are\n   302\t  Datalog over the rows: `yin.vm/free-names` today returns a symbol\n   303\t  set, and is extended (or wrapped by an occurrence-scoped query over\n   304\t  the same rules) to return each occurrence's path; the definitions\n   305\t  scanner is the store-key query behind `yin.vm/ast-requirements`\n   306\t  with the binding row's path and its enclosing tags; the application\n   307\t  scanner is the application-row query over the same relation. For\n   308\t  the vector formats all three are operand scans by pc (`:var`\n   309\t  against `:store-put`, `:load-free` against the `yin/def` call\n   310\t  sites, the call opcodes for applications) with conditional target\n   311\t  ranges taken from the `:jump-if` and body operands. A format whose\n   312\t  scanner returns positions as `nil` is admitted and falls under the\n   313\t  conservative degradation of step 5a: every occurrence is retained\n   314\t  as an obligation, and with no application positions no occurrence\n   315\t  inside a lambda body is discharged at all.\n   408\t5. **Verify dependency closure.** Two halves.\n   409\t   - *5a, at the linker: obligations.* Two scans run over the verified\n   410\t     value. `:obligations-fn` yields the free-name occurrences, each\n   411\t     with its position: for a tree, the occurrence path and whether it\n   412\t     lies inside a `:lambda` body; for a vector, the pc and whether it\n   413\t     lies in a body rather than the main sequence. `:definitions-fn`\n   414\t     yields the **definition set** with positions: every constant store\n   415\t     key the image binds at module level (the section 7.7 store-key\n   416\t     query of `yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md`: `:vm/store-put` rows,\n   417\t     `:store-put` operands, `yin/def` applications with a constant key),\n   418\t     each with the position of the binding in the main sequence.\n   419\t     A definition discharges an occurrence by **defined-before-use\n   420\t     under control-flow dominance**, not by subtraction of names and\n   421\t     not by source order alone. Source order says a definition is\n   422\t     written earlier; dominance says it has executed by the time the\n   423\t     occurrence runs. Only the second discharges, and where dominance\n   424\t     cannot be established the obligation is **retained**, never\n   425\t     dropped:\n   426\t     - A definition is *unconditional* when it sits in the main\n   427\t       sequence at top level or inside a `:do` (for a tree) or at a pc\n   428\t       in the main sequence outside every conditional target range\n   429\t       (for a vector); it is *conditional* when any `:if` branch, any\n   430\t       jump target, or any lambda body encloses it. A conditional\n   431\t       definition discharges nothing statically: the linker cannot know\n   432\t       the branch was taken, so an occurrence that depends on it keeps\n   433\t       its obligation and is checked at the receiver under 5b exactly\n   434\t       as an undefined name would be, and the manifest must declare it\n   435\t       or the link is `:undeclared-free`. This is conservative by\n   436\t       design: a module that defines a name only in one branch and\n   437\t       reads it afterwards must declare what the name means when the\n   438\t       branch is not taken.\n   439\t     - An occurrence in the main sequence (outside every lambda body)\n   440\t       is discharged only by an unconditional definition of that name\n   441\t       that dominates it: for a tree, an earlier sibling in the same\n   442\t       or an enclosing top-level `:do`; for a vector, an earlier pc in\n   443\t       the main sequence with no conditional target range between the\n   444\t       two. A main-sequence occurrence whose only definitions are all\n   445\t       later or all conditional and later is `:use-before-definition`:\n   446\t       in the isolated store it would read nothing, and no manifest\n   447\t       declaration may stand in for a name the module itself defines\n   448\t       unconditionally later. An occurrence whose only definitions are\n   449\t       conditional and earlier retains its obligation, per the rule\n   450\t       above.\n  1348\t    Nothing is written into any task's ambient store: this is\n  1349\t    7.6.2's \"there is no merge\" rule at the module grain -- a\n  1350\t    receiver binding of the same name can neither supply nor shadow\n  1351\t    the module's value.\n  1352\t  - *Run time.* While a closure carrying `:store-of m` executes, the\n  1353\t    module store of m is its **active store**: free reads resolve\n  1354\t    through it first and the receiver's free env, primitives, and\n  1355\t    registry second; the ambient store does not participate. Direct\n  1356\t    store instructions route by the same context -- `:store-put`\n  1357\t    (and the `:vm/store-put` effect) writes the active module\n  1358\t    store, and `:store-get` reads it with **no ambient fallback**:\n  1359\t    a key the module store lacks is absent, exactly as a top-level\n  1360\t    read of an absent key is; engine resources are unreachable\n  1361\t    either way, by the private-resource rule below. The context\n  1362\t    threads through calls: a frame records the caller's active\n  1363\t    `:store-of` (or none), applying a closure makes that closure's\n  1364\t    `:store-of` active, and returning restores the frame's, so a\n  1365\t    module closure calling another module's closure routes each\n  1366\t    body's reads and writes to its own module. A tail call that\n  1367\t    empties the continuation -- the closure's body was the whole\n  1368\t    computation -- clears the active context with the last frame,\n  1369\t    and the VM admits new top-level input only with no active\n  1370\t    context, which `yin.repl`'s append asserts, so input after a\n  1371\t    module closure applied never routes through a stale module\n  1372\t    store. Sibling exports in one task share one store instance,\n  1373\t    so a write one makes is visible to the next; each task holds\n  1374\t    its own instances, so writes never cross tasks. A declared\n  1375\t    obligation the store does not hold falls through to the\n  1376\t    receiver's bindings exactly as step 5b checked them; a\n  1377\t    conditional definition that ran overwrites the module's own\n  1378\t    slot, which is the publisher's semantics, not a shadow.\n    54\t(defn resolve-var\n    55\t  \"Look up a variable name: env -> store -> primitives -> module registry.\n    56\t\n    57\t   The registry is a value supplied by the composition, not a global.\"\n    58\t  [env store primitives registry name]\n    59\t  (if-let [pair (find env name)]\n    60\t    (val pair)\n    61\t    (if-let [pair (find store name)]\n    62\t      (val pair)\n    63\t      (if-let [pair (find primitives name)]\n    64\t        (vm/primitive-function (val pair))\n    65\t        (if-let [resolved (when (namespace name)\n    66\t                            (module/resolve-module\n    67\t                              registry\n    68\t                              (symbol (str (namespace name)\n    69\t                                           \".\"\n    70\t                                           (clojure.core/name name)))))]\n    71\t          resolved\n    72\t          (fail (str \"Unable to resolve symbol: \" name \" in this context\")\n    73\t                {:symbol name}))))))\n M src/cljc/yin/vm/content.cljc\n M src/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc\n M test/yin/vm/content_test.cljc\n M test/yin/vm/linker_test.cljc\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"Completed-GMT: 2026-09-25 11:06:02 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-09-25 18:06:02 Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh\n\nThe invocation-position fix is sound for the expander’s two-operand `yin/def` shape: the value operand precedes `[3 2]`, and the new test checks read-before-definition. The previously accepted application ordering, pre-hash byte cap, and zero-parts refusal remain intact. One shadowing gap blocks sign-off.\n\nP1 | [linker.cljc:446](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-ucf-phase2/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc:446) | The guard drops `yin/def`-derived definitions only when another `yin/def` application visibly binds `yin/def`. It misses a direct `:vm/store-put` of that name, despite scanning that row as a definition. It also cannot exclude a computed-key write that evaluates to `yin/def`. Runtime reads the active store before primitives ([engine.cljc:54](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-ucf-phase2/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:54)), so a subsequent apparent definition of `x` need not store `x`. The new fixture uses a `yin/def` rebinding, leaving both cases untested ([linker_test.cljc:150](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-ucf-phase2/test/yin/vm/linker_test.cljc:150)). | Treat every possible write to the module’s `yin/def` slot—including direct and unresolved computed-key writes—as invalidating syntactic `yin/def` definitions, or prove the primitive binding at each call. Add isolated tests for both writes.\n\nA different module’s store does not supply this shadow: the spec isolates each module’s active store ([spec:1352](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-ucf-phase2/docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md:1352)). The independent JVM, Node, and Dart runs match the reported counts, but do not cover the gap above.\n\nVerdict: REQUEST CHANGES\nSign-off: DENIED"}}
